# CLI build output (.fyp packages + checksum sidecars + unpacked runtime tree) — regenerated by
# `fengyu build`. Source lives in ui-src/ + src/; the generated typed RPC contracts under
# ui-src/src/generated/ and src/main/java/.../generated/ ARE committed (checked for drift by
# `fengyu check`), but the assembled dist/ packages are release artifacts.
dist-package/
dist/

# Aceternity components vendored per project by `fengyu add <slug> --yes` (toolchain 2.1.x
# stopped shipping them inside @infinia/plugin-ui). The Aceternity license forbids
# redistributing their source files — this repository is public, so the fetched files and
# the per-project license-ack marker must never be committed. Each machine (and CI) runs
# `fengyu add` once before `fengyu build`; see README.md "Aceternity components".
plugin-*/ui-src/src/aceternity/
plugin-*/ui-src/.fengyu-aceternity-ack
